  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"81\" data-end=\"343\">The <strong data-start=\"85\" data-end=\"109\">Filaria Antigen Test</strong> (commonly a <strong data-start=\"122\" data-end=\"165\">Circulating Filarial Antigen &ndash; CFA test</strong>) is used to detect <strong data-start=\"185\" data-end=\"235\">antigens released by live adult filarial worms</strong>, mainly <em data-start=\"244\" data-end=\"266\">Wuchereria bancrofti</em>. It is more specific than antibody tests and indicates <strong data-start=\"322\" data-end=\"342\">active infection</strong>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Positive</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates <strong>active infection</strong> with <em>Wuchereria bancrofti</em>. Adult filarial worms are present in the body. Immediate treatment is usually recommended.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Negative</strong></td>\n<td>No detectable circulating filarial antigen. Suggests <strong>no current active infection</strong>. However, it does <strong>not rule out</strong> early infection, low worm burden, or infection with species not detected by the test.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Weak Positive / Borderline</strong></td>\n<td>May indicate early or low-level infection. Repeat testing or confirmatory tests may be needed.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"990\" data-end=\"1022\"><strong data-start=\"994\" data-end=\"1022\">Clinical Considerations:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1024\" data-end=\"1407\">\n<li data-start=\"1024\" data-end=\"1152\">\n<p data-start=\"1026\" data-end=\"1152\">The test is <strong data-start=\"1038\" data-end=\"1065\">not dependent on timing</strong> of sample collection (unlike microfilaria smears that require night blood collection).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1153\" data-end=\"1276\">\n<p data-start=\"1155\" data-end=\"1170\">Can be used to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1173\" data-end=\"1276\">\n<li data-start=\"1173\" data-end=\"1209\">\n<p data-start=\"1175\" data-end=\"1209\">Diagnose <strong data-start=\"1184\" data-end=\"1209\">asymptomatic carriers</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1212\" data-end=\"1276\">\n<p data-start=\"1214\" data-end=\"1276\">Support <strong data-start=\"1222\" data-end=\"1267\">mass drug administration (MDA) monitoring</strong> programs</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1277\" data-end=\"1407\">\n<p data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1407\">Best used <strong data-start=\"1289\" data-end=\"1330\">in combination with clinical findings</strong> and, where available, <strong data-start=\"1353\" data-end=\"1379\">microfilaria detection</strong> (e.g., blood smear or PCR).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1414\" data-end=\"1434\"><strong data-start=\"1418\" data-end=\"1434\">Limitations:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1436\" data-end=\"1676\">\n<li data-start=\"1436\" data-end=\"1543\">\n<p data-start=\"1438\" data-end=\"1543\">The test primarily detects <strong data-start=\"1465\" data-end=\"1492\"><em data-start=\"1467\" data-end=\"1481\">W. bancrofti</em> antigens</strong>. It may <strong data-start=\"1501\" data-end=\"1531\">not detect <em data-start=\"1514\" data-end=\"1529\">Brugia malayi</em></strong> infections.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1544\" data-end=\"1605\">\n<p data-start=\"1546\" data-end=\"1605\">Cannot determine <strong data-start=\"1563\" data-end=\"1578\">worm burden</strong> or <strong data-start=\"1582\" data-end=\"1604\">stage of infection</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1606\" data-end=\"1676\">\n<p data-start=\"1608\" data-end=\"1676\">Antigen may remain detectable for <strong data-start=\"1642\" data-end=\"1675\">several weeks after treatment</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
